# LeadKart Go — Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Keep the build context small + secret-free. The Dockerfile uses
# `--mount=type=bind,target=.` so most of these aren't physically copied
# into image layers — but they ARE sent to the BuildKit daemon, so
# `*.env`, secrets, and IDE droppings still need filtering.
#
# Anything required at build time (go.mod, go.sum, internal/, cmd/,
# migrations/) is NOT excluded — the COPY rule chooses what lands.

# VCS + IDE + editors
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode
.editorconfig
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Local-only tooling — not needed for image build
.air.toml
.golangci.yml
Taskfile.yml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
lefthook.yml
.lefthook.yml

# Build + cache outputs
tmp/
bin/
dist/
.dockerignore
node_modules/
web/dist/

# Test artifacts
coverage.out
coverage-integration.out
coverage.html
*.coverprofile
junit-*.xml
**/*.test
**/testdata/

# Compose files — never want a compose definition leaking into the image,
# and the build only needs the Dockerfile itself.
docker/compose*.yml

# Secrets + envs (defence in depth — these MUST never reach a layer)
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Internal documentation — large + irrelevant at runtime
*.md
docs/
.claude/

# Goose / sqlc downloaded tools (in case `tool` directive caches locally)
.tools/
